<Window xmlns="clr-namespace:MGUI.Core.UI.XAML;assembly=MGUI.Core"
        Left="120" Top="80" Width="650" Height="700" TitleText="Component Measurement Test" Padding="10">
    <!--
    ComponentMeasureTest — Validation of MGElement.MeasureSelf component measurement
    ==================================================================================
    PURPOSE
    =======
    This sample verifies that the component measurement bug fix (Task 4) is correct:

    BUG FIXED (Bug 1): When multiple components share size with content via
    IsWidthSharedWithContent / IsHeightSharedWithContent, the old code summed
    all shared sizes. The fix uses element-wise MAX instead of SUM, so:

        OLD: FullSize = Unshared + Max(comp1 + comp2 + ..., Content)   ← wrong
        NEW: FullSize = Unshared + Max(Max(comp1, comp2, ...), Content) ← correct

    KNOWN REMAINING (Bug 2): Components cannot share their size with Padding.
    For elements where a component doesn't use the owner's padding (e.g. MGTabControl),
    the total is Sum(Padding, UnsharedComponent, Max(Content, SharedComponent))
    rather than Sum(Max(Padding, UnsharedComponent), Max(Content, SharedComponent)).
    This is documented but not yet fixed (requires more invasive changes).

    ASSERTIONS
    ==========
    Debug.Assert statements in MGElement.MeasureSelf verify that each component's
    measured size does not exceed the available space provided to it.
    These assertions fire in Debug builds whenever any element is measured.

    WHAT TO CHECK VISUALLY
    ======================
    - The MGListBox shows its title bar and its item list, with the header and list
      aligned to the same width (both fill the box horizontally).
    - The MGTabControl shows its tab headers and content panel correctly aligned.
    - Neither element has unexpected extra whitespace or misaligned borders.
    - The measurement labels at the bottom show the calculated component sizes.
    -->

    <Window.Styles>
        <Style TargetType="TextBlock">
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="10" />
        </Style>
        <Style Name="Header1" TargetType="TextBlock">
            <Setter Property="IsBold" Value="True" />
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="13" />
        </Style>
        <Style TargetType="Separator">
            <Setter Property="Margin" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="Height" Value="2" />
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="White" />
            <Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0.25" />
        </Style>
    </Window.Styles>

    <ScrollViewer VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto" Background="rgb(60,60,60)" Padding="6,4">
        <StackPanel Orientation="Vertical" Spacing="12">

            <TextBlock StyleNames="Header1" Text="Component Measurement Test" HorizontalAlignment="Center" />
            <Separator/>

            <TextBlock>
                This sample validates the [c=Turquoise]MeasureSelf[/c] fix for component measurement.
                [b]Bug 1[/b] (FIXED): shared component sizes now use [c=Yellow]MAX[/c] instead of [c=Red]SUM[/c].
                Each [c=Turquoise]Debug.Assert[/c] in [c=Turquoise]MeasureSelf[/c] verifies component size ≤ available size.
            </TextBlock>
            <Separator/>

            <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════
                 SCENARIO 1: ListBox with title
                 (OuterBorder + TitleComponent + InnerBorderComponent,
                  Title and InnerBorder both IsWidthSharedWithContent=true)
                 ═══════════════════════════════════════ -->
            <TextBlock StyleNames="Header1" Text="Scenario 1 — MGListBox" />
            <TextBlock>
                The [c=Turquoise]MGListBox[/c] has three components: an outer border, a title bar component
                (IsWidthSharedWithContent=[c=Yellow]true[/c]), and an inner border component
                (IsWidthSharedWithContent=[c=Yellow]true[/c]).
                With the fix, both shared-width components contribute via MAX, not SUM.
                Verify that the title bar and item list have the same width.
            </TextBlock>

            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="10" HorizontalAlignment="Left">
                <!-- ListBox without explicit size, with title — should size to content -->
                <ListBox Name="TestListBox1" IsTitleVisible="True" OuterBB="rgba(255,200,50,255)" OuterBT="2"
                         xmlns:System="clr-namespace:System;assembly=mscorlib" ItemType="{x:Type System:String}">
                    <ListBox.Header>
                        <TextBlock Text="Test List Box" Foreground="White" IsBold="True" />
                    </ListBox.Header>
                    <System:String>Item Alpha</System:String>
                    <System:String>Item Beta</System:String>
                    <System:String>Item Gamma - a longer item to test width</System:String>
                    <System:String>Item Delta</System:String>
                    <System:String>Item Epsilon</System:String>
                </ListBox>

                <!-- ListBox with explicit width, with title — both header and list fill it -->
                <ListBox Name="TestListBox2" IsTitleVisible="True" Width="200" OuterBB="rgba(50,200,255,255)" OuterBT="2"
                         xmlns:System="clr-namespace:System;assembly=mscorlib" ItemType="{x:Type System:String}">
                    <ListBox.Header>
                        <TextBlock Text="Fixed Width List" Foreground="White" IsBold="True" />
                    </ListBox.Header>
                    <System:String>Short item</System:String>
                    <System:String>Another item</System:String>
                    <System:String>Third item</System:String>
                </ListBox>
            </StackPanel>
            <TextBlock Name="ListBoxMeasureLabel" Text="ListBox measurement: ..." Foreground="Yellow" />
            <Separator/>

            <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════
                 SCENARIO 2: TabControl
                 ═══════════════════════════════════════ -->
            <TextBlock StyleNames="Header1" Text="Scenario 2 — MGTabControl" />
            <TextBlock>
                The [c=Turquoise]MGTabControl[/c] has one component: a border component
                (IsWidthSharedWithContent=[c=Yellow]false[/c], IsHeightSharedWithContent=[c=Yellow]false[/c]).
                This verifies that single-component elements continue to work correctly with the fix.
                [c=Gray](Bug 2 — Padding sharing — affects TabControl but is not yet fixed.)[/c]
            </TextBlock>

            <TabControl Name="TestTabControl" Width="400" Height="200">
                <TabItem Header="Tab One">
                    <StackPanel Orientation="Vertical" Spacing="4" Padding="6">
                        <TextBlock Text="Content of Tab One" />
                        <TextBlock Text="This verifies component measurement in TabControl." />
                    </StackPanel>
                </TabItem>
                <TabItem Header="Tab Two">
                    <StackPanel Orientation="Vertical" Spacing="4" Padding="6">
                        <TextBlock Text="Content of Tab Two" />
                    </StackPanel>
                </TabItem>
                <TabItem Header="Tab Three — Longer Header">
                    <StackPanel Orientation="Vertical" Spacing="4" Padding="6">
                        <TextBlock Text="Content of Tab Three" />
                    </StackPanel>
                </TabItem>
            </TabControl>
            <TextBlock Name="TabControlMeasureLabel" Text="TabControl measurement: ..." Foreground="Yellow" />
            <Separator/>

            <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════
                 SCENARIO 3: Custom element with two shared-width components
                 Represented by a TextBox (has CharacterCount + TextBlock components,
                 both partially shared)
                 ═══════════════════════════════════════ -->
            <TextBlock StyleNames="Header1" Text="Scenario 3 — MGTextBox (multi-component)" />
            <TextBlock>
                [c=Turquoise]MGTextBox[/c] has 5 components including shared-width ones
                (CharacterCount component: IsWidthSharedWithContent=[c=Yellow]true[/c]).
                Verify that the text box renders correctly and doesn't have measurement artifacts.
            </TextBlock>

            <TextBox Name="TestTextBox1" Width="300" ShowCharacterCount="True" CharacterLimit="50"
                     Placeholder="Type here to test measurement..." BorderBrush="rgba(200,100,255,255)" BorderThickness="2" />
            <TextBlock Name="TextBoxMeasureLabel" Text="TextBox measurement: ..." Foreground="Yellow" />
            <Separator/>

            <!-- Live measurement display -->
            <TextBlock StyleNames="Header1" Text="Live Measurement Info" />
            <TextBlock>
                The following labels display the [c=Turquoise]LayoutBounds[/c] and
                [c=Yellow]Padding[/c] of each test element, updated every frame.
                These confirm the fix produces correct measured sizes.
            </TextBlock>
            <StackPanel Orientation="Vertical" Background="Black * 0.3" Padding="6" Spacing="3">
                <TextBlock Name="Info_LB1" Text="ListBox1 LayoutBounds: ..." />
                <TextBlock Name="Info_LB2" Text="ListBox2 LayoutBounds: ..." />
                <TextBlock Name="Info_TC"  Text="TabControl LayoutBounds: ..." />
                <TextBlock Name="Info_TB1" Text="TextBox1 LayoutBounds: ..." />
            </StackPanel>

        </StackPanel>
    </ScrollViewer>
</Window>
